{"id":"COR-1","class":"correctness","severity":"blocking","file":"src/ui/views/order-view.js","line":279,"what_breaks":"A failed line save (quota) can show no visible error on a long order. The banner goes to the page region under the h1, not to the top of the line form panel. Focus then moves straight back to Save, so the browser scrolls away from the banner. The form looks as if Save did nothing.","requirement":"R-21","evidence":"Input: an order with about 20 lines (each row at least 2.75rem) and full storage. onSubmit line 277 commit fails, line 279 showBanner, main.js line 64 querySelector('[data-banner-region]') finds the only region, which sits under the h1 (order-view.js line 335); formHolder has none. main.js line 65 focuses the banner, then order-view.js line 280 ui.save.focus() scrolls back to the form after the total line, below all rows. UI-SPEC 7.6 says 'a failed save keeps the form open with a banner at the top of its panel'.","proven":true},
{"id":"COR-2","class":"correctness","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/views/order-view.js","line":320,"what_breaks":"Deleting an order while a dirty line form is open asks 'Discard your changes?' after the delete has already happened. Keep editing leaves the deleted order on screen. Its Cancel then throws and shows APP-01; its Save line replaces the screen with not-found and drops the typed text.","requirement":"R-08","evidence":"Delete order is not disabled while the form is open (only addButton and the row buttons take ui.open, lines 74-75, 206). Input: open Add line, type 'x', Delete order, confirm. confirmDelete line 315 commits, line 320 location.replace('#/orders') does not clear state.form. main.js onHashChange line 184 sees form.isDirty() true and calls askToDiscard. onSafe line 175 restores the hash of the deleted order, and render is skipped because it equals renderedHash. Cancel: cancelForm, closeForm, drawLines line 205 currentOrder() is undefined, line 207 now.lines throws TypeError, APP-01.","proven":true},
{"id":"COR-3","class":"correctness","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/views/order-view.js","line":237,"what_breaks":"Keep editing throws when focus was last on Save line or Cancel in the line form. The user gets APP-01 telling them to reload, and reloading loses the typed text. The normal R-21 path reaches this: a failed save, then leaving to delete data as the message advises.","requirement":"R-21","evidence":"Lines 217-219 store event.target.id on focusin, and Save line and Cancel have no id (components.js actionButton), so ui.lastFocused becomes ''. Line 280 ui.save.focus() sets this on every failed save. Input: dirty line form, failed save, click Orders, Keep editing. main.js line 176 calls restoreFocus, line 237 document.getElementById('') returns null, .focus() throws TypeError, the window error listener shows APP-01. The route forms guard this with 'lastFocused ? ... : ...'; the line form does not.","proven":true},
{"id":"COR-4","class":"correctness","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/views/order-view.js","line":283,"what_breaks":"After a failed line save or Remove, a successful retry leaves the danger banner on screen. The page says 'so this was not saved' for a change that was saved.","requirement":"R-21","evidence":"Input: a Save line or Remove fails with STO-01, the user frees space, and the retry succeeds. Lines 283-284 (closeForm, addButton.focus) and lines 298-299 (drawLines, addButton.focus) touch only linesHolder, totalHolder and formHolder. Nothing empties the banner region created at line 335. UI-SPEC section 6: 'a banner leaves when its cause is gone'.","proven":true},
{"id":"COR-5","class":"correctness","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/views/customer-list.js","line":114,"what_breaks":"A newly saved customer does not appear in the list when an older search text is still active. The user lands on 'No customers match this search.' straight after saving.","requirement":"R-01","evidence":"Input: search 'zzz', open New customer, save 'Ana'. customer-form.js line 116 goes to #/customers, line 114 reads the retained state.searchCustomers, searchCustomers filters Ana out. ADR-005 line 46 keeps the text between screens on purpose, while R-01 says 'then the customer appears in the list'. The conflict between the two needs a decision.","proven":true},
